# k8s/taxcalc-api/taxcalc-api.rollout.yaml.disabled
#
# W6 D5 lands this.
#
# Produced by the W6 D2 `argocd-author` audit pass:
#
#   /argocd-author taxcalc-api --namespace-prefix taxcalc --strategy canary --secrets-mode eso
#
# The generator scaffolded a Rollout before Argo Rollouts was installed. That
# is CORRECT behaviour for `--strategy canary`, not a defect, so this artefact
# is kept rather than discarded - "the CRD is missing" is an argument about
# when to apply something, not about whether it is the right thing to apply.
# It is commented out (and the file carries a .disabled suffix so Kustomize
# cannot pick it up even if someone adds a glob to k8s/taxcalc-api/kustomization.yaml)
# because applying it today fails three separate ways:
#
#   1. No argoproj.io/Rollout CRD on this cluster - the API server rejects it.
#   2. `Rollout` and `AnalysisTemplate` are absent from the AppProject's
#      namespaceResourceWhitelist, so the sync would be denied even with the
#      CRD present. The generator added both; adopt that change WITH the
#      install, not before it.
#   3. A Rollout and the existing Deployment both select
#      app.kubernetes.io/name=taxcalc-api. Two controllers owning one pod set
#      fight indefinitely. k8s/taxcalc-api/taxcalc-api.deployment.yaml must be removed
#      from k8s/taxcalc-api/kustomization.yaml in the same commit that enables this.
#
# The AnalysisTemplate query is the W5 D5 success-rate SLI. W6 D5 gates the
# canary on p99 latency, which needs the multi-arch build first: the dev image
# currently runs under binfmt emulation at ~8-9x idle CPU, and a p99 measured
# against an emulated binary says nothing about production. See the emulation
# section above.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
# kind: Rollout
# metadata:
